From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 10:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] Recovery Calendar, Volume Heatmap, Smart Exercise Swap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three high-leverage visual/utility features built on existing data; no schema
change, no new analytics engines.

- domain/swap/ExerciseSwapEngine.kt: offline alternatives for a lift — same
  primary muscle via same movement pattern, equipment-diversified, with an
  optional 'unavailable equipment' filter. Surfaced in the Exercise Library
  detail dialog ('Swap / alternatives'); ExerciseViewModel exposes
  swapSuggestions for the selected exercise.
- domain/recovery/RecoveryCalendar.kt: per-day green/amber/red readiness from
  training density (back-to-back/heavy => recovering, moderate => caution,
  rested => ready). Shown as a 14-day strip on the Training DNA screen.
- Volume Heatmap: a colour-coded muscle-group grid reusing the existing
  VolumeLandmarks data, on the Training DNA screen.
- TrainingDnaViewModel now also produces recoveryCalendar; heatmap reuses
  volumeLandmarks.

Verified: full domain compiles on kotlinc 1.9.22 (192 classes); 6 logic tests
pass in-sandbox (swap same-movement/diversify/empty, calendar ready/recovering/
no-data). No conflict markers; FlowRow opt-in added. No tests committed.
